## Final configuration — `/etc/nginx/nginx.conf`

```nginx
user www-data;
worker_processes 1;
pid /run/nginx.pid;
error_log /tmp/inventory-nginx-error.log notice;

events {
    worker_connections 512;
}

http {
    access_log /tmp/inventory-nginx-access.log;
    keepalive_timeout 10;

    server {
        listen 127.0.0.1:8443 ssl;
        server_name localhost;

        ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;
        ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/tls/server.crt;
        ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/tls/server.key;
        ssl_client_certificate /etc/nginx/tls/ca.crt;
        ssl_verify_client off;

        location = /health {
            root /srv/inventory;
            try_files /health.json =404;
            default_type application/json;
        }

    }
}
```

**Change made:** `ssl_verify_client on;` → `ssl_verify_client off;` — HTTPS (TLS 1.2/1.3) is retained on `127.0.0.1:8443`, but a client certificate is no longer required. The `ssl_client_certificate` / trusted CA chain (`/etc/nginx/tls/ca.crt`) is kept in place, so clients that still present the trusted cert are accepted.

## Actions performed
1. Baseline check: no-cert request was rejected with HTTP 400 (mTLS enforced).
2. Edited `ssl_verify_client` to `off`.
3. `nginx -t` — syntax and test successful.
4. `nginx -s reload` — graceful reload; master process stayed up (PID 16), loopback HTTPS service continuously running.

